A||||4||1FieroGTRacingInc||Missing Ground???||||5||
Z||000000||1FieroGTRacingInc||01-29-2001||12:36 PM||||My 86SE-v6 ....  no headlight's, interior light's barely<BR> work at all, and no fuel pressure , I can hear my relay click but no pressure??? new battery too.  I think that when I installed this motor awhile ago I must have missed a ground wire right??<BR>These problem's just started all of a sudden, this motor was firing and idling fine.. Now I noticed the no fuel pressure first... then the light's, now that's why I was thinking a ground wire or strap.<P>------------------<BR>1FieroGTRacingInc.||||reg||5
Z||000001||1FieroGTRacingInc||01-29-2001||12:56 PM||||anyone know how many and where the ground's should connect, or be checked????  thank's for any help..  Steve<P>------------------<BR>1FieroGTRacingInc.||||reg||1
Z||000002||TheFiero64||01-29-2001||12:59 PM||||It sounds like it could be. I would take a cable and run it from the neg(-) Terminal of the batt to a good spot on the chassis of the car and see if it is ok then. If it is then follow the Neg. cable to where it is mounted to the engine and check for a ground strap that runs to the decklid hinge.<P>Don't rule out the batt being low.||||reg||1
Z||000003||1FieroGTRacingInc||01-29-2001||01:46 PM||||Yes it was the strap from the motor to the decklid hinge...  lol I came across it looking through a box of both part's from the swap, and came across both brass strap's...  lol  feel stupid now...  thank's.<P>------------------<BR>1FieroGTRacingInc.||||reg||1
Z||000004||TheFiero64||01-29-2001||02:17 PM||||Glad I could help  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
